  "body": "Stacked on #3834 (merge #3834 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- `contour_link::ring_entry` now applies on the wall side too. On the wall side it applies to the Ramp and Helix arms only.\n- `contour::emit_band` calls `ring_entry` for each untabbed ring after the first ring of a level, inside or outside.\n- An outside ring after another ring now goes through `engage_level`. It takes the wall-side ramp of #3833 (`contour_wall_ramp`).\n- The helix stands down to that ramp. It says so in its one existing note.\n- The traverse between the parts rides the pass link plane (`Step::traverse` from #3834). Pass `Clearance` crosses at `clearance_z`. Pass `Retract` crosses at the hop plane.\n- These stay as before:\n  - the wall-side Arc entry (its own hop and wall arc);\n  - tabbed levels;\n  - the Plunge entry;\n  - a `KeepDown` pass link that holds its proof (it feeds straight across);\n  - a ring that is too short for the ramp angle (it grazes, with the existing \"too short\" note).\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3917-contour-outside-ring-entry.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`ring_entry` returned `None` on the wall side. Thus each ring after the first ring at a level took `ring_link`. That link lifts, crosses and plunges straight down at the plunge feed. It posts no note.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe pin uses the `outside_ramped` fixture: tool 10 mm, stepdown 1 mm, 3 levels, bottom Z -3, ramp 5 degrees, 16 mm square parts 40 mm apart.\n\n| Entry | 2 parts (before / after) | 3 parts (before / after) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ramp 5 deg, axial dives | 3 / 0 | 6 / 0 |\n| Plunge, axial dives | 6 / 6 | 9 / 9 |\n\nBefore the fix, the notes were empty (`[]`).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `every_outside_ring_of_several_parts_is_entered_by_the_wall_side_ramp` (`camcraft-motion`, `tests/machining2d.rs`).\n  - It covers 2 and 3 parts, Ramp and Helix, and pass `Clearance` and pass `Retract`.\n  - It asserts: no axial dive, no `Plunge` move, the steepest descent is at most 5 degrees, and each ring-to-ring crossing rides the pass link plane.\n- Red before the fix: yes. On the #3834 head the pin fails: `2 parts, Ramp, pass Clearance: no ring dives: []`, left 3, right 0.\n- Mutation: I put back `ring_to_ring && inside && !tabbed` at the call site. The pin fails with the same message. I restored the fix. The pin passes.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: 43 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `camcraft-app` suites `example_catalog` (41 pass, 4 ignored heavy), `example_catalog_adaptive` (1 pass), `example_catalog_edge_work` (1 pass).\n- Heavy lanes: not run. This is a `P3` PR. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a heavy step only to a `P1` PR.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. I ran the example catalog suites above. No `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No end-to-end app or post test with several outside parts. The pin is at the motion level.\n- No UI change, so no screenshots.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Stacked on #3834. It changes the same functions: `contour::emit_band` (the `ring_entry` call) and `contour_link::ring_entry`. Retarget is not needed: this PR already targets `main`. Merge #3834 first.\n- #3912 touches `crates/motion/tests/machining2d.rs`, in other tests. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: 2D Contour outside: each ring after the first ring at a level is now entered by the Ramp or Helix entry, not by an axial plunge with no note.\n\nFixes #3917\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
